{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7pHGF3ygf3TD77yTtM9pY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd062-touch\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/touch: Create Files and Update Timestamps\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts and build systems use touch to create empty files and update file timestamps.\n6\t  The macOS BSD touch differs from GNU touch in -d date string parsing and --time flag\n7\t  behavior. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtouch,\n8\t  installed by coreutils) in file creation, timestamp modification, and exit codes for all\n9\t  supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Create empty files that do not exist.\n13\t  - G2: Update access and modification timestamps of existing files.\n14\t  - G3: Support explicit timestamp specification via -t, -d, and -r.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Default behavior and file creation\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: When given one or more FILE arguments, must update the access and modification times of each file to the current time.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: When a named file does not exist, must create it as an empty file with default permissions.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: \"-c or --no-create must suppress file creation. If the file does not exist, must not create it and must not report an error.\"\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must support multiple file arguments, processing each in order.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Timestamp selection and explicit times\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-a must change only the access time.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: \"-m must change only the modification time.\"\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: \"When neither -a nor -m is given, must change both access and modification times.\"\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"-t STAMP must use the timestamp [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss] instead of the current time.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Reference file and date string\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: \"-r FILE or --reference=FILE must use the timestamps of FILE instead of the current time.\"\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: \"-d STRING or --date=STRING must parse the date string and use it instead of the current time.\"\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: \"When a reference file does not exist, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\"\n50\t      - R3.4:\n51\t          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must affect the symbolic link itself rather than the file it points to.\"\n52\t\n53\t  R4:\n54\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n55\t    items:\n56\t      - R4.1:\n57\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n58\t      - R4.2:\n59\t          text: Must exit 1 when an error occurs (invalid timestamp, missing reference file, permission denied). Must continue processing remaining files after an error.\n60\t      - R4.3:\n61\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file timestamps between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n62\t      - R4.4:\n63\t          text: \"Tests must cover: create new file, update existing file, -c no-create, -a access only, -m modification only, -t explicit timestamp, -d date string, -r reference file, multiple files, and error cases (invalid timestamp, missing reference file).\"\n64\t\n65\tnon_goals:\n66\t  - cmd/touch does not implement the obsolescent -t format with two-digit years outside the [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss] specification.\n67\t  - cmd/touch does not implement --time=WORD as a standalone flag (it is an alias for -a/-m in GNU touch but rarely used).\n68\t\n69\tacceptance_criteria:\n70\t  - id: AC1\n71\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch /tmp/newfile creates the file if absent, matching gtouch.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.4\n76\t  - id: AC2\n77\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -c /tmp/nonexistent does not create the file and exits 0, matching gtouch.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.3\n80\t      - R4.1\n81\t  - id: AC3\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -t 202401151030.00 /tmp/testfile sets the timestamp, matching gtouch.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R2.3\n85\t      - R2.4\n86\t      - R4.1\n87\t  - id: AC4\n88\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -r /tmp/reffile /tmp/testfile copies timestamps, matching gtouch.\"\n89\t    traces:\n90\t      - R3.1\n91\t      - R3.3\n92\t  - id: AC5\n93\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gtouch passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n94\t    traces:\n95\t      - R4.3\n96\t      - R4.4\n97\t  - id: AC6\n98\t    criterion: \"cmd/touch compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n99\t    traces:\n100\t      - R1.1\n101\t      - R1.2\n102\t      - R1.3\n103\t      - R1.4\n104\t      - R2.1\n105\t      - R2.2\n106\t      - R2.3\n107\t      - R2.4\n108\t      - R3.1\n109\t      - R3.2\n110\t      - R3.3\n111\t      - R3.4\n112\t      - R4.1\n113\t      - R4.2\n114\t      - R4.3\n115\t      - R4.4\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31c12309-51d3-4723-8331-36ed2107f1db","uuid":"20edfbef-ba88-4142-bdfd-c3eabeb099b3","timestamp":"2026-05-21T18:16:34.226Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5431/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd062-touch.yaml","content":"id: srd062-touch\ntitle: \"cmd/touch: Create Files and Update Timestamps\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts and build systems use touch to create empty files and update file timestamps.\n  The macOS BSD touch differs from GNU touch in -d date string parsing and --time flag\n  behavior. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gtouch,\n  installed by coreutils) in file creation, timestamp modification, and exit codes for all\n  supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Create empty files that do not exist.\n  - G2: Update access and modification timestamps of existing files.\n  - G3: Support explicit timestamp specification via -t, -d, and -r.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior and file creation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When given one or more FILE arguments, must update the access and modification times of each file to the current time.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: When a named file does not exist, must create it as an empty file with default permissions.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-c or --no-create must suppress file creation. If the file does not exist, must not create it and must not report an error.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must support multiple file arguments, processing each in order.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Timestamp selection and explicit times\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-a must change only the access time.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-m must change only the modification time.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"When neither -a nor -m is given, must change both access and modification times.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-t STAMP must use the timestamp [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss] instead of the current time.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Reference file and date string\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-r FILE or --reference=FILE must use the timestamps of FILE instead of the current time.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-d STRING or --date=STRING must parse the date string and use it instead of the current time.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"When a reference file does not exist, must print an error to stderr and exit 1.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must affect the symbolic link itself rather than the file it points to.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when an error occurs (invalid timestamp, missing reference file, permission denied). Must continue processing remaining files after an error.\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file timestamps between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: create new file, update existing file, -c no-create, -a access only, -m modification only, -t explicit timestamp, -d date string, -r reference file, multiple files, and error cases (invalid timestamp, missing reference file).\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/touch does not implement the obsolescent -t format with two-digit years outside the [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss] specification.\n  - cmd/touch does not implement --time=WORD as a standalone flag (it is an alias for -a/-m in GNU touch but rarely used).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch /tmp/newfile creates the file if absent, matching gtouch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -c /tmp/nonexistent does not create the file and exits 0, matching gtouch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.3\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -t 202401151030.00 /tmp/testfile sets the timestamp, matching gtouch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/touch -r /tmp/reffile /tmp/testfile copies timestamps, matching gtouch.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gtouch passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"cmd/touch compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
