{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via a cobbler orchestrator system) assigned stitch task #5431 to implement srd062-touch requirements R2.1-R2.4 in the go-unix-utils project. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: `-a` must change only the access time\n   - R2.2: `-m` must change only the modification time\n   - R2.3: When neither `-a` nor `-m` is given, must change both access and modification times\n   - R2.4: `-t STAMP` must use the timestamp `[[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss]` instead of the current time\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/touch/main.go` (extend implementation) and `cmd/touch/touch_test.go` (add differential tests). Acceptance criteria require successful build, vet, and test passes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `touch` utility, verified via differential testing against `gtouch` (Homebrew coreutils)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for differential testing comparing Go binary output vs reference binary\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` required at start of main\n   - `os.Chtimes(path, atime, mtime)` for setting file timestamps\n   - Timestamp parsing for `[[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss]` format\n   - When `-a` only: must preserve existing modification time (need to stat the file first)\n   - When `-m` only: must preserve existing access time (need to stat the file first)\n   - `pkg/sys.Stat` or `pkg/sys.Lstat` provides `FileInfo` with `AccessTime`, `ModTime`, `ChangeTime`\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - E8 constitution: no function may exceed 40 lines\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd062-touch.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements R2.1-R2.4\n     - R2.1: `-a` changes only access time\n     - R2.2: `-m` changes only modification time\n     - R2.3: When neither `-a` nor `-m`, change both\n     - R2.4: `-t STAMP` uses `[[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss]` format\n     - Non-goals: no obsolescent -t two-digit year format, no `--time=WORD` standalone flag\n\n   - **cmd/touch/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently implements only R1.1-R1.4 (basic touch with -c/--no-create)\n     - Key existing functions:\n       ```go\n       func main() {\n           sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n           noCreate, files, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n           // ...\n           os.Exit(run(noCreate, files))\n       }\n       \n       func run(noCreate bool, files []string) int {\n           exitCode := 0\n           now := time.Now()\n           for _, path := range files {\n               if err := touchFile(path, noCreate, now); err != nil {\n                   fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"touch: %s\\n\", err)\n                   exitCode = 1\n               }\n           }\n           return exitCode\n       }\n       \n       func touchFile(path string, noCreate bool, t time.Time) error {\n           _, err := os.Stat(path)\n           if os.IsNotExist(err) {\n               if noCreate { return nil }\n               f, createErr := os.Create(path)\n               if createErr != nil {\n                   return fmt.Errorf(\"cannot touch '%s': %s\", path, sysMsg(createErr))\n               }\n               f.Close()\n           }\n           if err := os.Chtimes(path, t, t); err != nil {\n               return fmt.Errorf(\"cannot touch '%s': %s\", path, sysMsg(err))\n           }\n           return nil\n       }\n       \n       func parseArgs(args []string) (bool, []string, error) {\n           // Only handles -c and --no-create currently\n       }\n       \n       func parseShortFlags(flags string, noCreate *bool) error {\n           // Only handles 'c' character\n       }\n       \n       func parseLongFlag(flag 